<title>BRAZIL: Brazil aluminium output down 4.3 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Brazil aluminium output down 4.3 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian production of primary aluminium totalled 91,000 tonnes in February, Brazilian Aluminium Association (ABAL) said in a statement.</p>
<p>That was 4.3 percent lower than February 1996 output of 95,100 tonnes.</p>
<p>Production in the first two months of this year reached 191,200 tonnes, a fall of 2.4 percent on the 196,000 tonnes produced in January/February 1996.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
